    </edge>
    <edge source="James E. Gunn" target="sentences" id="0">
      <data key="d12">CREATED</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">I came across some sentences by science-fiction writer and critic, James Gunn</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Isaac" target="Foundation series" id="0">
      <data key="d12">CREATED</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">The Foundation series had been written at a time when our knowledge of astronomy was primitive compared with what it is today.</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Isaac" target="Foundations at Bay" id="0">
      <data key="d12">CREATED</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">I suggested Foundations at Bay, therefore, and that may be the title that will actually be used.</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Isaac" target="Hugh O'Neill" id="0">
      <data key="d12">WORKS_FOR</data>
      <data key="d13">0.8</data>
      <data key="d14">I brought the manuscript to Hugh O'Neill in batches, and the poor fellow went half-crazy since he insisted on reading it in this broken fashion.</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Foundation's Edge" target="Editor's note" id="0">
      <data key="d12">MENTIONED_IN</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">Editor's note: The novel was published in October 1982 as Foundation's Edge.</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Gaal Dornick" target="Encyclopedia Galactica" id="0">
      <data key="d12">MENTIONED_IN</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">The best existing authority we have for the details of his life is the biography written by Gaal Dornick</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Gaal Dornick" target="Raven Seldon" id="0">
      <data key="d12">KNOWS</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">The best existing authority we have for the details of his life is the biography written by Gaal Dornick who. as a young man, met Seldon two years before the great mathematician's death.</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Gaal Dornick" target="Synnax" id="0">
      <data key="d12">LOCATED_IN</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">Even though he had lived all his life on the world of Synnax</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Gaal Dornick" target="Seldon Project" id="0">
      <data key="d12">PARTICIPATES_IN</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">an invitation from the great Hari Seldon to come to Trantor and join the vast and somewhat mysterious Seldon Project</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Gaal Dornick" target="space-tour" id="0">
      <data key="d12">PARTICIPATES_IN</data>
      <data key="d13">0.7</data>
      <data key="d14">Why don't you take a space-tour once you hit Trantor.</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Gaal Dornick" target="ship landing" id="0">
      <data key="d12">PARTICIPATES_IN</data>
      <data key="d13">0.8</data>
      <data key="d14">The ship landed in a medley of noises.</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Gaal Dornick" target="Trantor" id="0">
      <data key="d12">LOCATED_IN</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">This was Trantor!</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Gaal Dornick" target="airflight" id="0">
      <data key="d12">PARTICIPATES_IN</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">Gaal stared out the curved, transparent window, marvelling at the sensation of airflight within an enclosed structure</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Gaal Dornick" target="Direct line to the Luxor" id="0">
      <data key="d12">PARTICIPATES_IN</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">A man in glaring blue and yellow uniform, shining and new in unstainable plasto-textile, reached for his two bags. "Direct line to the Luxor," he said. The man who followed Gaal heard that. He also heard Gaal say, "Fine," and watched him enter the blunt-nosed vehicle.</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Gaal Dornick" target="University of Trantor" id="0">
      <data key="d12">PARTICIPATES_IN</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">He would have to be at the University tomorrow.</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Gaal Dornick" target="elevator ride" id="0">
      <data key="d12">PARTICIPATES_IN</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">Gaal entered and others flowed in behind him. The operator closed a contact. For a moment, Gaal felt suspended in space as gravity switched to zero, and then he had weight again in small measure as the elevator accelerated upward.</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Gaal Dornick" target="observation tower visit" id="0">
      <data key="d12">PARTICIPATES_IN</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">Here's your ticket. Special elevator in the rear. It's marked 'To the Tower.' Just take it.</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Gaal Dornick" target="Jerril" id="0">
      <data key="d12">KNOWS</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">His friend of the elevator was indicating a seat next to himself and Gaal took it. The man smiled. "My name is Jerril."</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Gaal Dornick" target="Psychohistory" id="0">
      <data key="d12">WORKS_FOR</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">I came here primarily for a job." "Oh?" Gaal felt obliged to explain further, "With Dr. Seldon's project at the University of Trantor."</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Gaal Dornick" target="Psychohistory" id="1">
      <data key="d12">MENTIONED_IN</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">That trial is described in Gaal Dornick's biography of Hari Seldon.</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Gaal Dornick" target="Hari Seldon" id="0">
      <data key="d12">KNOWS</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">"I am Hari Seldon," an instant before Gaal's befuddled brain placed the face alongside the memory of the many times he had seen it in pictures.</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Gaal Dornick" target="Dr. Seldon's staff" id="0">
      <data key="d12">WORKS_FOR</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">He had applied for a position on Dr. Seldon's staff and had been accepted.</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Gaal Dornick" target="conversation" id="0">
      <data key="d12">PARTICIPATES_IN</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">we were able to overhear your conversation with Dr. Seldon</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Gaal Dornick" target="provinces" id="0">
      <data key="d12">LOCATED_IN</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">You are from the provinces.</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Gaal Dornick" target="trial" id="0">
      <data key="d12">PARTICIPATES_IN</data>
      <data key="d13">0.8</data>
      <data key="d14">The trial (Gaal supposed it to be one, though it bore little resemblance legalistically to the elaborate trial techniques Gaal had read of) had not lasted long.</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Gaal Dornick" target="project" id="0">
      <data key="d12">PARTICIPATES_IN</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">Q. Including Dr. Gaal Dornick? A. Dr. Dornick is the fifty-first,</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Gaal Dornick" target="hearings" id="0">
      <data key="d12">PARTICIPATES_IN</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">The next day's hearings were entirely different. Hari Seldon and Gaal Dornick were alone with the Commission.</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Gaal Dornick" target="exile" id="0">
      <data key="d12">PARTICIPATES_IN</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">Then need you have accepted exile</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Gaal Dornick" target="psychohistoric findings" id="0">
      <data key="d12">PARTICIPATES_IN</data>
      <data key="d13">0.7</data>
      <data key="d14">I never lie about psychohistoric findings.</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Gaal Dornick" target="martial law" id="0">
      <data key="d12">PARTICIPATES_IN</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">You and your men will be under martial law henceforth.</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Encyclopedia Galactica" target="Encyclopedia Galactica Publishing Co." id="0">
      <data key="d12">CREATED</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">All quotations from the Encyclopedia Galactica here reproduced are taken from the 116th Edition published in 1020 F.E. by the Encyclopedia Galactica Publishing Co.</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Raven Seldon" target="psychohistory" id="0">
      <data key="d12">CREATED</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">Undoubtedly his greatest contributions were in the field of psychohistory. Seldon found the field little more than a set of vague axioms; he left it a profound statistical science.</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Raven Seldon" target="Foundation series" id="0">
      <data key="d12">MENTIONED_IN</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">file:///F|/rah/Isaac%20Asimov/Foundation.txt</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Raven Seldon" target="calculator pad" id="0">
      <data key="d12">CREATED</data>
      <data key="d13">0.8</data>
      <data key="d14">Seldon removed his calculator pad from the pouch at his belt.</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Raven Seldon" target="trial of Hari Seldon" id="0">
      <data key="d12">MENTIONED_IN</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">In a way, the beginning of the Commission's decline can be traced to the trial of Hari Seldon two years before the beginning of the Foundational Era.</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Raven Seldon" target="EVENT" id="0">
      <data key="d12">PARTICIPATES_IN</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">The Advocate flushed and interrupted Seldon.</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Raven Seldon" target="trial" id="0">
      <data key="d12">PARTICIPATES_IN</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">The tale of my interrupted trial will spread through the Galaxy.</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Raven Seldon" target="exile" id="0">
      <data key="d12">PARTICIPATES_IN</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">Seldon said, "I accept exile."</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Raven Seldon" target="Trantor" id="0">
      <data key="d12">WORKS_FOR</data>
      <data key="d13">0.7</data>
      <data key="d14">and meanwhile, doctor, you will not trouble Trantor</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Raven Seldon" target="followers" id="0">
      <data key="d12">LEADS</data>
      <data key="d13">0.8</data>
      <data key="d14">The alternative is death for yourself and for as many of your followers as will seem necessary.</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Raven Seldon" target="psychohistoric findings" id="0">
      <data key="d12">PARTICIPATES_IN</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">I never lie about psychohistoric findings.</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Raven Seldon" target="University of Trantor" id="0">
      <data key="d12">WORKS_FOR</data>
      <data key="d13">0.7</data>
      <data key="d14">the taxi whined through the hundreds of miles of worm-like tunnels toward the University.</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Raven Seldon" target="martial law" id="0">
      <data key="d12">PARTICIPATES_IN</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">You and your men will be under martial law henceforth.</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Raven Seldon" target="Gaal Dornick" id="0">
      <data key="d12">KNOWS</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">Gaal turned to Seldon</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Raven Seldon" target="Terminus" id="0">
      <data key="d12">WORKS_FOR</data>
      <data key="d13">0.8</data>
      <data key="d14">–to be exiled to Terminus? Why not?</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Raven Seldon" target="plan" id="0">
      <data key="d12">CREATED</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">in a plan such as ours, the actions of others are bent to our needs</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Raven Seldon" target="Imperial" id="0">
      <data key="d12">WORKS_FOR</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">Working on Terminus, we will have Imperial support</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Raven Seldon" target="scientific refuge" id="0">
      <data key="d12">LEADS</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">a scientific refuge will be established on Terminus</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Raven Seldon" target="revolt on Anacreon" id="0">
      <data key="d12">PARTICIPATES_IN</data>
      <data key="d13">0.8</data>
      <data key="d14">instigate the revolt on Anacreon at the right time and in the right manner</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Raven Seldon" target="Commissioners on Trantor" id="0">
      <data key="d12">MANEUVERED</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">Seldon maneuvered the Commissioners on Trantor into ordering the Foundation established on Terminus.</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Raven Seldon" target="Anacreonian mess" id="0">
      <data key="d12">MENTIONED_IN</data>
      <data key="d13">0.7</data>
      <data key="d14">if he foresaw the Anacreonian mess</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Raven Seldon" target="Plan" id="0">
      <data key="d12">CREATED</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">There's Hari Seldon and the Plan, you know.</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Raven Seldon" target="The Foundation" id="0">
      <data key="d12">CREATED</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">The Foundation, as he says, was established as a scientific refuge</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Raven Seldon" target="Time Vault" id="0">
      <data key="d12">MENTIONED_IN</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">Hari Seldon said in the Time Vault</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Raven Seldon" target="advanced psychology" id="0">
      <data key="d12">CREATED</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">Because even Seldon's advanced psychology was limited.</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Raven Seldon" target="law of mob psychology" id="0">
      <data key="d12">MENTIONED_IN</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">Seldon wanted us to proceed blindly – and therefore correctly – according to the law of mob psychology.</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Empire" target="Trantor" id="0">
      <data key="d12">LOCATED_IN</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">owed allegiance to the Empire whose seat was on Trantor</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Empire" target="Foundation series" id="0">
      <data key="d12">MENTIONED_IN</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">file:///F|/rah/Isaac%20Asimov/Foundation.txt</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Empire" target="quadrillion human beings" id="0">
      <data key="d12">LEADS</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">an Empire that has stood for twelve thousand years, through all the vicissitudes of the generations, and which has behind it the good wishes and love of a quadrillion human beings</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Empire" target="passage" id="0">
      <data key="d12">MENTIONED_IN</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">The Empire will vanish and all its good with it.</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Empire" target="treaty" id="0">
      <data key="d12">PARTICIPATES_IN</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">a copy of the treaty between the Empire and Anacreon</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Empire" target="nuclear technicians are scarce" id="0">
      <data key="d12">COMPLAINS</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">Empire complains that nuclear technicians are scarce.</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Empire" target="ships" id="0">
      <data key="d12">OWNS</data>
      <data key="d13">0.8</data>
      <data key="d14">Jael, they're getting ships from the Empire itself.</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Empire" target="Galactic center" id="0">
      <data key="d12">LOCATED_IN</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">in the Galactic center it's still very much alive</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Empire" target="Galaxy" id="0">
      <data key="d12">LOCATED_IN</data>
      <data key="d13">0.8</data>
      <data key="d14">in whole sectors of the Galaxy</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Empire" target="The Foundation" id="0">
      <data key="d12">ENEMY_OF</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">The whole war is a battle between those two systems, between the Empire and the Foundation</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Trantor" target="Empire" id="0">
      <data key="d12">LOCATED_IN</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">owed allegiance to the Empire whose seat was on Trantor</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Trantor" target="Galactic center" id="0">
      <data key="d12">LOCATED_IN</data>
      <data key="d13">0.8</data>
      <data key="d14">The stars were thick here near the Galactic center.</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Trantor" target="space-tour" id="0">
      <data key="d12">MENTIONED_IN</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">Why don't you take a space-tour once you hit Trantor.</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Trantor" target="central regions of the Galaxy" id="0">
      <data key="d12">LOCATED_IN</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">located, as it was, toward the central regions of the Galaxy</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Trantor" target="center of the Imperial Government" id="0">
      <data key="d12">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">As the center of the Imperial Government for unbroken hundreds of generations</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Trantor" target="the system" id="0">
      <data key="d12">LOCATED_IN</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">among the most densely populated and industrially advanced worlds of the system</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Trantor" target="Galactic Empire" id="0">
      <data key="d12">LOCATED_IN</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">the impossibility of proper administration of the Galactic Empire under the uninspired leadership of the later Emperors was a considerable factor in the Fall.</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Trantor" target="outer worlds" id="0">
      <data key="d12">DEPENDENT_ON</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">Its dependence upon the outer worlds for food and, indeed, for all necessities of life, made Trantor increasingly vulnerable to conquest by siege.</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Trantor" target="Galaxy" id="0">
      <data key="d12">LOCATED_IN</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">the planet which was the center of all the Galaxy</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Trantor" target="sub-ocean soil" id="0">
      <data key="d12">LOCATED_IN</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">It even works itself out a few miles into the sub-ocean soil at the shorelines.</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Trantor" target="Total destruction" id="0">
      <data key="d12">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">Gaal said, unbelievingly, "Total destruction! But – but that is impossible. Trantor has never been –"</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Trantor" target="conversation" id="0">
      <data key="d12">MENTIONED_IN</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">He is of the opinion that Trantor would be destroyed within three centuries</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Trantor" target="hands of the aristocratic families" id="0">
      <data key="d12">LOCATED_IN</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">Trantor, I am afraid is in the hands of the aristocratic families</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Trantor" target="ruins" id="0">
      <data key="d12">LOCATED_IN</data>
      <data key="d13">0.8</data>
      <data key="d14">Trantor will lie in ruins</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Trantor" target="Imperial Government" id="0">
      <data key="d12">LOCATED_IN</data>
      <data key="d13">0.8</data>
      <data key="d14">Let me suggest to you that your predictions of disaster might be intended to destroy public confidence in the Imperial Government for purposes of your own.</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Trantor" target="passage" id="0">
      <data key="d12">MENTIONED_IN</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">You said earlier that you could not prevent the destruction of Trantor;</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Trantor" target="Encyclopedia Galactica" id="0">
      <data key="d12">MENTIONED_IN</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">But by the time Trantor falls, it will be complete and copies will exist in every major library in the Galaxy.</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Trantor" target="Imperial Library" id="0">
      <data key="d12">LOCATED_IN</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">Trantor, my lord, possesses the Imperial Library</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Trantor" target="University of Trantor" id="0">
      <data key="d12">LOCATED_IN</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">as well as the scholarly resources of the University of Trantor</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Spaceship-and-Sun" target="Empire" id="0">
      <data key="d12">MEMBER_OF</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">the white uniform with the Spaceship-and-Sun of the Empire on it</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Spaceship-and-Sun" target="weapons" id="0">
      <data key="d12">MENTIONED_IN</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">The butts of those weapons had, deeply etched upon them, in worn gold plating, the Spaceship-and-Sun!</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Spaceship-and-Sun" target="Encyclopedia" id="0">
      <data key="d12">MENTIONED_IN</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">The same Spaceship-and-Sun that was stamped on every. one of the great volumes of the original Encyclopedia that the Foundation had begun and not yet finished.</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Spaceship-and-Sun" target="Galactic Empire" id="0">
      <data key="d12">MENTIONED_IN</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">The same Spaceship-and-Sun that had blazoned the banner of the Galactic Empire through millennia.</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Luxor Hotel" target="Trantor" id="0">
      <data key="d12">LOCATED_IN</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">"The Luxor Hotel," said the driver, unnecessarily.</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="University of Trantor" target="Trantor" id="0">
      <data key="d12">LOCATED_IN</data>
      <data key="d13">0.8</data>
      <data key="d14">The University structures lacked the hard steel-gray of the rest of Trantor.</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Emperor's palace" target="world" id="0">
      <data key="d12">LOCATED_IN</data>
      <data key="d13">0.8</data>
      <data key="d14">Somewhere on the world, he realized vaguely, was the Emperor's palace</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Jerril" target="Gaal Dornick" id="0">
      <data key="d12">KNOWS</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">His friend of the elevator was indicating a seat next to himself and Gaal took it. The man smiled. "My name is Jerril."</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Jerril" target="Commission of Public Safety" id="0">
      <data key="d12">MEMBER_OF</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">He is an agent of the Commission of Public Safety.</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Psychohistory" target="passage" id="0">
      <data key="d12">MENTIONED_IN</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">Listen with the ears of psychohistory, and you will hear the creaking.</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Commission of Public Safety" target="trial of Hari Seldon" id="0">
      <data key="d12">MENTIONED_IN</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">In a way, the beginning of the Commission's decline can be traced to the trial of Hari Seldon two years before the beginning of the Foundational Era.</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Commission of Public Safety" target="Gaal Dornick" id="0">
      <data key="d12">DETAINS</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">he was under detention at the orders of the Commission of Public Safety.</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Commission of Public Safety" target="aristocratic families" id="0">
      <data key="d12">MEMBER_OF</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">Trantor, I am afraid is in the hands of the aristocratic families, members of which compose the Commission of Public Safety.</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Commission of Public Safety" target="trial" id="0">
      <data key="d12">MENTIONED_IN</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">Five of the Commission of Public Safety sat behind the raised desk.</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Emperor Cleon I" target="assassination of Cleon I" id="0">
      <data key="d12">MENTIONED_IN</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">The aristocratic coterie rose to power after the assassination of Cleon I, last of the Entuns.</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Emperor Cleon I" target="Entuns" id="0">
      <data key="d12">FAMILY_OF</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">The aristocratic coterie rose to power after the assassination of Cleon I, last of the Entuns.</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Chens" target="aristocratic coterie" id="0">
      <data key="d12">MEMBER_OF</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">Usually under the control of the great families of the Chens and the Divarts, it degenerated eventually into a blind instrument for maintenance of the status quo.</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Divarts" target="aristocratic coterie" id="0">
      <data key="d12">MEMBER_OF</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">Usually under the control of the great families of the Chens and the Divarts, it degenerated eventually into a blind instrument for maintenance of the status quo.</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Avakim" target="conversation" id="0">
      <data key="d12">PARTICIPATES_IN</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">The Commission will, of course, have a spy beam on our conversation.</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Avakim" target="Gaal Dornick" id="0">
      <data key="d12">KNOWS</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">Avakim approached, nodded to Gaal</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Avakim" target="Hari Seldon" id="0">
      <data key="d12">KNOWS</data>
      <data key="d13">0.7</data>
      <data key="d14">Avakim approached, nodded to Gaal, leaned over to whisper to Seldon.</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="members" target="Commission of Public Safety" id="0">
      <data key="d12">MEMBER_OF</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">members of which compose the Commission of Public Safety</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Commission" target="Hari Seldon" id="0">
      <data key="d12">ENEMY_OF</data>
      <data key="d13">0.8</data>
      <data key="d14">The Commission has been more and more hostile to his activities</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Linge Chen" target="Commission of Public Safety" id="0">
      <data key="d12">MEMBER_OF</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">In the center was the Chief Commissioner Linge Chen.</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Linge Chen" target="Commission" id="0">
      <data key="d12">LEADS</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">Linge Chen said, "I will speak," and the other Commissioners sat back in their chairs, prepared to listen.</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Linge Chen" target="Galaxy" id="0">
      <data key="d12">LEADS</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">Chen, lean and hard, older in looks than in fact, was the actual Emperor of all the Galaxy.</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Chen" target="Hari Seldon" id="0">
      <data key="d12">KNOWS</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">Chen said, "Dr. Seldon, you disturb the peace of the Emperor's realm."</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Chen" target="personal domain of his august majesty, the Emperor" id="0">
      <data key="d12">WORKS_FOR</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">Chen said, "Dr. Seldon, you disturb the peace of the Emperor's realm."</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Chen" target="Foundation series" id="0">
      <data key="d12">MENTIONED_IN</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">said Chen. Negligently, he turned the papers upon his desk with his fingertips so that they faced Seldon.</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Chen" target="Raven Seldon" id="0">
      <data key="d12">KNOWS</data>
      <data key="d13">0.8</data>
      <data key="d14">Chen knew I spoke the truth.</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Chen" target="plan" id="0">
      <data key="d12">MENTIONED_IN</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">Chen's temperamental makeup has been subjected to greater scrutiny</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="personal domain of his august majesty, the Emperor" target="Empire" id="0">
      <data key="d12">LEADS</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">We are under the direct control of the Emperor himself</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="personal domain of his august majesty, the Emperor" target="Board of Trustees" id="0">
      <data key="d12">LEADS</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">the Board of Trustees, simply because it is the Board of Trustees acting in the name of the Emperor</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Terminus" target="Galaxy" id="0">
      <data key="d12">LOCATED_IN</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">It is at the edge of the Galaxy, sir.</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Terminus" target="Galactic spiral" id="0">
      <data key="d12">LOCATED_IN</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">Located on the very fringe of the Galactic spiral</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Terminus" target="Empire" id="0">
      <data key="d12">LOCATED_IN</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">We are part of the Emperor's personal domain</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Terminus" target="strategic spot" id="0">
      <data key="d12">LOCATED_IN</data>
      <data key="d13">0.8</data>
      <data key="d14">Terminus occupies an extremely strategic spot</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Terminus" target="Anacreon" id="0">
      <data key="d12">LOCATED_IN</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">since Terminus cannot defend itself, Anacreon must take over the job for its own sake.</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Terminus" target="planet" id="0">
      <data key="d12">LOCATED_IN</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">Terminus is a planet practically without metals.</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Terminus" target="Encyclopedists" id="0">
      <data key="d12">MEMBER_OF</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">Terminus is not a planet, but a scientific foundation preparing a great encyclopedia.</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Terminus" target="Encyclopedists" id="1">
      <data key="d12">LOCATED_IN</data>
      <data key="d13">0.8</data>
      <data key="d14">we found ourselves a world of scientists concentrated in a single city</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Terminus" target="metals" id="0">
      <data key="d12">LACK_OF</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">lack of metals on Terminus</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Terminus" target="Periphery" id="0">
      <data key="d12">LOCATED_IN</data>
      <data key="d13">0.8</data>
      <data key="d14">Here in the Periphery they've lost nuclear power.</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Terminus" target="Foundation series" id="0">
      <data key="d12">LOCATED_IN</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">file:///F|/rah/Isaac%20Asimov/Foundation.txt</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Terminus" target="crisis" id="0">
      <data key="d12">PARTICIPATES_IN</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">it is the present crisis that is starting Terminus off to that climax</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Terminus" target="Renascence" id="0">
      <data key="d12">PARTICIPATES_IN</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">the seeds of the Renascence and the future founders of the Second Galactic Empire</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Terminus" target="Galactic Empire" id="0">
      <data key="d12">LOCATED_IN</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">the planet, Terminus, had trafficked with every part of the Galactic Empire</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Terminus" target="Kingdoms" id="0">
      <data key="d12">LOCATED_IN</data>
      <data key="d13">0.8</data>
      <data key="d14">You have helped rebuild power plants on their territories.</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Terminus" target="Kingdoms" id="1">
      <data key="d12">WORKS_FOR</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">you have carried out a policy of scientific aid to the Kingdoms.</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Terminus" target="nuclear power" id="0">
      <data key="d12">OWNS</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">You have given them nuclear power.</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Terminus" target="medical clinics" id="0">
      <data key="d12">OWNS</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">You have established medical clinics, chemical laboratories and factories.</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Terminus" target="chemical laboratories" id="0">
      <data key="d12">OWNS</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">You have established medical clinics, chemical laboratories and factories.</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Terminus" target="factories" id="0">
      <data key="d12">OWNS</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">You have established medical clinics, chemical laboratories and factories.</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Terminus" target="ships of their navies" id="0">
      <data key="d12">SERVICES</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">actually serviced the ships of their navies</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Terminus" target="The Foundation" id="0">
      <data key="d12">LOCATED_IN</data>
      <data key="d13">0.7</data>
      <data key="d14">Wienis who had one hour earlier declared him a prisoner of war and Terminus on the point of destruction</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Terminus" target="five million homes" id="0">
      <data key="d12">LOCATION</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">In five million homes on Terminus, excited observers crowded their receiving sets more closely,</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Encyclopedists" target="landing" id="0">
      <data key="d12">PARTICIPATES_IN</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">until the landing of the Encyclopedists</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Lewis Pirenne" target="Encyclopedia Foundation Number One" id="0">
      <data key="d12">WORKS_FOR</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">to establish themselves and set up Encyclopedia Foundation Number One into a smoothly working unit</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Lewis Pirenne" target="Board of Trustees" id="0">
      <data key="d12">LEADS</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">He is the Chairman of the Board of Trustees</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Lewis Pirenne" target="Chairman of the Board of Trustees" id="0">
      <data key="d12">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">He is the Chairman of the Board of Trustees</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Lewis Pirenne" target="personal representative of the Emperor" id="0">
      <data key="d12">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">a personal representative of the Emperor</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Lewis Pirenne" target="Haut Rodric" id="0">
      <data key="d12">ENEMY_OF</data>
      <data key="d13">0.8</data>
      <data key="d14">Pirenne and Haut Rodric – having met with loud and mutual protestations of esteem and regard – were detesting each other's company a good deal more</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Lewis Pirenne" target="scientific institution" id="0">
      <data key="d12">WORKS_FOR</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">As a scientific institution–</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Salvor Hardin" target="Pirenne" id="0">
      <data key="d12">KNOWS</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">Hardin smiled to himself. He was in a hurry, but he knew better than to take offense at Pirenne's cavalier treatment of anything or anyone that disturbed him at his work.</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Salvor Hardin" target="City Council meeting" id="0">
      <data key="d12">PARTICIPATES_IN</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">I promised to be back at the City Council meeting before the new aqueduct project is put to a vote.</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Salvor Hardin" target="state occasion" id="0">
      <data key="d12">PARTICIPATES_IN</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">Salvor Hardin at the spaceport with all the imposing ritual of a state occasion.</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Salvor Hardin" target="Lee" id="0">
      <data key="d12">KNOWS</data>
      <data key="d13">0.7</data>
      <data key="d14">Lee's men were in control and the Board was giving orders no longer.</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Salvor Hardin" target="Lee" id="1">
      <data key="d12">HATES</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">"Good-by, Lee. I hate to leave you in the frying pan like this, but there's not another I can trust."</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Salvor Hardin" target="Haut Rodric" id="0">
      <data key="d12">KNOWS</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">Salvor Hardin had guessed since the day that Anselm haut Rodric had first revealed to him</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Salvor Hardin" target="Anacreon" id="0">
      <data key="d12">LEADS</data>
      <data key="d13">0.8</data>
      <data key="d14">the strange society forced temporarily upon it during the administration of Salvor Hardin</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Salvor Hardin" target="Anacreon" id="1">
      <data key="d12">ENEMY_OF</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">since the utter rout of Anacreon</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Salvor Hardin" target="Yohan Lee" id="0">
      <data key="d12">KNOWS</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">Yohan Lee advocated extreme measures. "I don't see, Hardin," he said</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Salvor Hardin" target="Yohan Lee" id="1">
      <data key="d12">FRIENDS_WITH</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">"Yes, I know that. I suppose that's why you're the one man I trust."</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Salvor Hardin" target="coup against the Encyclopedists" id="0">
      <data key="d12">PARTICIPATES_IN</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">we engineered our coup against the Encyclopedists way back</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Salvor Hardin" target="The Foundation" id="0">
      <data key="d12">LEADS</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">"Yes, Lepold, the leader of the Foundation himself is coming to Anacreon on your birthday"</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Salvor Hardin" target="The Foundation" id="1">
      <data key="d12">MEMBER_OF</data>
      <data key="d13">0.7</data>
      <data key="d14">stopping only long, enough to confer with the local representatives of the Foundation</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Salvor Hardin" target="Lepold I" id="0">
      <data key="d12">ENEMY_OF</data>
      <data key="d13">0.8</data>
      <data key="d14">"It is the same Salvor Hardin, who on his previous visit, ground our noses into the dust."</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Salvor Hardin" target="coronation" id="0">
      <data key="d12">PARTICIPATES_IN</data>
      <data key="d13">0.8</data>
      <data key="d14">It was only on the day before the coronation that he arrived</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Salvor Hardin" target="Terminus" id="0">
      <data key="d12">WORKS_FOR</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">Salvor Hardin, mayor of Terminus</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Salvor Hardin" target="Terminus" id="1">
      <data key="d12">LEADS</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">the mayor of Terminus</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Salvor Hardin" target="Time Vault" id="0">
      <data key="d12">PARTICIPATES_IN</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">Salvor Hardin compared this large company with the few men attending the first appearance of Hari Seldon, thirty years earlier.</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Salvor Hardin" target="City Council" id="0">
      <data key="d12">WORKS_FOR</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">Every man of the City Council was awaiting Seldon's appearance. He, himself, was still mayor</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Salvor Hardin" target="passage" id="0">
      <data key="d12">MENTIONED_IN</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">Since Salvor Hardin's time, the primacy and the mayoralty have never been combined in a single person.</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Salvor Hardin" target="priesthood" id="0">
      <data key="d12">USED</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">Salvor Hardin used the priesthood and the superstition of the people to overthrow the independence and power of the secular monarchs.</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Salvor Hardin" target="superstition of the people" id="0">
      <data key="d12">USED</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">Salvor Hardin used the priesthood and the superstition of the people to overthrow the independence and power of the secular monarchs.</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Salvor Hardin" target="Foundation series" id="0">
      <data key="d12">MENTIONED_IN</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">Hober Mallow took his place next to Hari Seldon and Salvor Hardin in the hearts of the people of the Foundation.</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Pirenne" target="Encyclopedia" id="0">
      <data key="d12">WORKS_FOR</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">The Encyclopedia takes up all my time.</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Pirenne" target="Encyclopedia" id="1">
      <data key="d12">MEMBER_OF</data>
      <data key="d13">0.8</data>
      <data key="d14">Our policy has but one cardinal principle, and that is the Encyclopedia.</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Pirenne" target="Board of Trustees" id="0">
      <data key="d12">MEMBER_OF</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">the Board of Trustees of the Encyclopedia Committee has been given full administrative powers</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Pirenne" target="Board of Trustees" id="1">
      <data key="d12">LEADS</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">Pirenne, himself, presiding</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Pirenne" target="personal domain of his august majesty, the Emperor" id="0">
      <data key="d12">WORKS_FOR</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">I am the Emperor's representative on Terminus, Hardin, and have full powers in this respect.</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Pirenne" target="Hardin" id="0">
      <data key="d12">KNOWS</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">Pirenne and Hardin onto the balcony</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Pirenne" target="Foundation series" id="0">
      <data key="d12">MENTIONED_IN</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">Pirenne tried again.</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Pirenne" target="Journal" id="0">
      <data key="d12">MENTIONED_IN</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">Information to this effect has been given the Journal.</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Pirenne" target="EVENT" id="0">
      <data key="d12">MENTIONED_IN</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">Pirenne sipped at the glass of water before him by way of preparation and said</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Pirenne" target="The Foundation" id="0">
      <data key="d12">MENTIONED_IN</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">agreed Pirenne.</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Pirenne" target="The Foundation" id="1">
      <data key="d12">WORKS_FOR</data>
      <data key="d13">0.8</data>
      <data key="d14">And he nodded to Pirenne, who responded with a delighted bow.</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Pirenne" target="Board" id="0">
      <data key="d12">MEMBER_OF</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">"Very true," agreed Pirenne.</data>
