    </edge>
    <edge source="Termin" target="no trained psychologists" id="0">
      <data key="d12">LOCATED_IN</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">There are no trained psychologists on Terminus</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Lepold I" target="Wienis" id="0">
      <data key="d12">FAMILY_OF</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">Wienis stood upon the threshold of his chambers and beetled at his young nephew.</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Lepold I" target="Anacreon" id="0">
      <data key="d12">LEADS</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">Lepold, you are king of Anacreon.</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Lepold I" target="Lepold's grandfather" id="0">
      <data key="d12">FAMILY_OF</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">at the very beginning of the reign of your grandfather</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Lepold I" target="King Lepold" id="0">
      <data key="d12">FAMILY_OF</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">It had been your father's hope, before his untimely death</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Lepold I" target="Ambassador Verisof" id="0">
      <data key="d12">KNOWS</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">You've been listening to Verisof quite a bit, I take it.</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Lepold I" target="Ambassador Verisof" id="1">
      <data key="d12">ENEMY_OF</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">Verisof, next to Salvor Hardin, is your greatest enemy.</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Lepold I" target="war against the Foundation" id="0">
      <data key="d12">LEADS</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">you must take an active part in ordering the war against the Foundation.</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Lepold I" target="Salvor Hardin" id="0">
      <data key="d12">ENEMY_OF</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">Verisof, next to Salvor Hardin, is your greatest enemy.</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Lepold I" target="coming of age" id="0">
      <data key="d12">PARTICIPATES_IN</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">Lepold is coming of age next week</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Lepold I" target="people" id="0">
      <data key="d12">LEADS</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">Lepold gives the order and the people fight</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Lepold I" target="kingdom" id="0">
      <data key="d12">LEADS</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">for the king stood apart in lonely and impressive grandeur</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Lepold I" target="Foundation series" id="0">
      <data key="d12">MENTIONED_IN</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">he had been introduced to Lepold as one of a long line of introducees</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Lepold I" target="EVENT" id="0">
      <data key="d12">PARTICIPATES_IN</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">Lepold sat on it now, hands solidly on its arms, head high, face frozen.</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Lepold I" target="Hardin" id="0">
      <data key="d12">ENEMY_OF</data>
      <data key="d13">0.8</data>
      <data key="d14">Lepold followed, wide-eyed, scared speechless. "Hardin," said Wienis, huskily, "you are playing with forces too great for you."</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ship" target="passage" id="0">
      <data key="d12">MENTIONED_IN</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">I've been to the ship today.</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Lewis Bort" target="Action Party" id="0">
      <data key="d12">MEMBER_OF</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">Lewis Bort was the most active in rallying those dissident elements which had fused into the now-vociferous Action Party.</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Lewis Bort" target="Anacreon" id="0">
      <data key="d12">LOCATED_IN</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">He was absent for the very good reason that he was on Anacreon's capital world at the time.</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Lewis Bort" target="vote of confidence" id="0">
      <data key="d12">PARTICIPATES_IN</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">They had joined in the vote of confidence</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Bort" target="Sef Sermak" id="0">
      <data key="d12">KNOWS</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">There was silence all round and all eyes turned to Sermak. The young party leader was biting a fingernail nervously, and then said loudly, "No good. It's fishy!" He looked around him, and added more energetically, "Is Hardin then such a fool?" "Seems to be," shrugged Bort.</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="priesthood" target="instruments of science" id="0">
      <data key="d12">CONTROL_OF</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">The priesthood has sole control of the instruments of science we have given Anacreon</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Levi Norast" target="PERSON" id="0">
      <data key="d12">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d13">1.0</data>
      <data key="d14">Levi Norast stamped in</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Actionist Party" target="City Council" id="0">
      <data key="d12">MEMBER_OF</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">the fifty-nine members of the Actionist Party reared upon their hind legs and stamped out of the Council Chambers.</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="palace guards" target="EVENT" id="0">
      <data key="d12">PARTICIPATES_IN</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">palace guards had streamed into the darkness.</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Theo Aporat" target="Anacreon" id="0">
      <data key="d12">MEMBER_OF</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">Theo Aporat was one of the very highest ranking priests of Anacreon.</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Theo Aporat" target="The Foundation" id="0">
      <data key="d12">WORKS_FOR</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">He had worked directly under the holy men from the Foundation itself in repairing the ship.</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Theo Aporat" target="Anacreonian navy" id="0">
      <data key="d12">MEMBER_OF</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">as represented by our ... priest-attendant, Theo Aporat</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Prince Lefkin" target="Wienis" id="0">
      <data key="d12">FAMILY_OF</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">And it was the son of this same Wienis that was the admiral who five minutes before had told him: "Attend to your souls and your blessings, priest. I will attend to my ship."</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Prince Lefkin" target="Aporat" id="0">
      <data key="d12">HATES</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">The admiral stared at the priest-attendant with hating eyes.</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Prince Lefkin" target="the ship" id="0">
      <data key="d12">LEADS</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">"I am commander here."</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Prince Lefkin" target="regent" id="0">
      <data key="d12">FAMILY_OF</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">There had been one startled gasp from the regent at the haggard face and shredded uniform of his son,</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Aporat" target="royal flagship Wienis" id="0">
      <data key="d12">WORKS_FOR</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">The head priest-attendant had the right of free entry anywhere on the ship.</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Aporat" target="general communications room" id="0">
      <data key="d12">LEADS</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">He had entered the general communications room now. His acolyte preceded him and the two officers in charge made no move to interfere.</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Aporat" target="sacrilege" id="0">
      <data key="d12">PARTICIPATES_IN</data>
      <data key="d13">0.8</data>
      <data key="d14">"Your ship," he cried, "is engaged in sacrilege.</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Aporat" target="commander" id="0">
      <data key="d12">ENEMY_OF</data>
      <data key="d13">0.8</data>
      <data key="d14">It is the intention of your commander to take this ship to the Foundation and there to bombard that source of all blessings into submission to his sinful will.</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Aporat" target="Galactic Spirit" id="0">
      <data key="d12">MEMBER_OF</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">I, in the name of the Galactic Spirit, remove him from his command, for there is no command where the blessing of the Galactic Spirit has been withdrawn.</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Aporat" target="The Foundation" id="0">
      <data key="d12">MEMBER_OF</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">the holy men of the Foundation</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Aporat" target="EVENT" id="0">
      <data key="d12">PARTICIPATES_IN</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">such curses as that of Aporat's are really deadly</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Aporat" target="EVENT" id="1">
      <data key="d12">LEADS</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">Aporat saw the darkness close down on the ship</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Aporat" target="Prince Lefkin" id="0">
      <data key="d12">KNOWS</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">He found Prince Lefkin, groping his way through the officers' quarters, cursing loudly for lights.</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Aporat" target="Prince Lefkin" id="1">
      <data key="d12">ENEMY_OF</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">The admiral stared at the priest-attendant with hating eyes.</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Aporat" target="noble admiral" id="0">
      <data key="d12">ENEMY_OF</data>
      <data key="d13">0.8</data>
      <data key="d14">Aporat interrupted furiously. "Seize the blasphemer. You listen to him at the peril of your souls." And promptly, the noble admiral went down under the clutching hands of a score of soldiers.</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Aporat" target="soldiery" id="0">
      <data key="d12">LEADS</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">Aporat turned, and with Lefkin dragged along after him, and the corridors behind black with soldiery, he returned to the communications room.</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="noble admiral" target="Siwenna" id="0">
      <data key="d12">ENEMY_OF</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">So while the people were still gathered in every large city, cheering the Emperor and his admiral, he occupied all armed centers, and then ordered the population put to the nuclear blast.</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Lefkin" target="return to Anacreon" id="0">
      <data key="d12">PARTICIPATES_IN</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">Order the rest of the fleet to cease course and to prepare for the return to Anacreon.</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Lefkin" target="Wienis' chambers" id="0">
      <data key="d12">MENTIONED_IN</data>
      <data key="d13">0.8</data>
      <data key="d14">There was absolute silence in Wienis' chambers when the image of Prince Lefkin appeared at the televisor.</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Traders" target="Empire" id="0">
      <data key="d12">PARTICIPATES_IN</data>
      <data key="d13">0.8</data>
      <data key="d14">Through it all they forged an empire more enduring than the pseudo-religious despotism of the Four Kingdoms</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Traders" target="The Foundation" id="0">
      <data key="d12">MENTIONED_IN</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">and constantly in advance of the political hegemony of the Foundation were the Traders</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Limmar Ponyets" target="shower" id="0">
      <data key="d12">PARTICIPATES_IN</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">Limmar Ponyets was completely a-lather when the call reached his receiver</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Limmar Ponyets" target="call" id="0">
      <data key="d12">PARTICIPATES_IN</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">when the call reached his receiver</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Limmar Ponyets" target="Galactic Periphery" id="0">
      <data key="d12">LOCATED_IN</data>
      <data key="d13">0.8</data>
      <data key="d14">even in the dark, hard space of the Galactic Periphery</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Limmar Ponyets" target="Gorm" id="0">
      <data key="d12">KNOWS</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">"What've you been doing, Gorm?" he asked, darkly.</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Limmar Ponyets" target="Eskel Gorov" id="0">
      <data key="d12">KNOWS</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">Limmar Ponyets was one of the few people who happened to know that Master Trader Eskel Gorov</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Limmar Ponyets" target="The Foundation" id="0">
      <data key="d12">WORKS_FOR</data>
      <data key="d13">0.8</data>
      <data key="d14">They expelled me, for reasons sufficient to promote me to a secular education under the Foundation</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Gorm" target="trade" id="0">
      <data key="d12">PARTICIPATES_IN</data>
      <data key="d13">0.7</data>
      <data key="d14">a second trade ship was alongside, and a grinning youngster entered through the air tube between the ships</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Les Gorm" target="Ponyets" id="0">
      <data key="d12">KNOWS</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">"What've you been doing, Gorm?" he asked, darkly.</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Les Gorm" target="Guild" id="0">
      <data key="d12">MEMBER_OF</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">"It will bear telling, since you're of the Guild."</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Ponyets" target="Guild" id="0">
      <data key="d12">MEMBER_OF</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">"It will bear telling, since you're of the Guild."</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Ponyets" target="Askone" id="0">
      <data key="d12">PARTICIPATES_IN</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">"I've got to go to Askone."</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Ponyets" target="The Foundation" id="0">
      <data key="d12">WORKS_FOR</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">an agent of the Foundation</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Ponyets" target="The Foundation" id="1">
      <data key="d12">PARTICIPATES_IN</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">But I'm out to make money, and this is my chance. If it helps the Foundation at the same time, all the better.</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Ponyets" target="EVENT" id="0">
      <data key="d12">PARTICIPATES_IN</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">Ponyets strode to the foot of the Chair of State</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Ponyets" target="Eskel Gorov" id="0">
      <data key="d12">KNOWS</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">Eskel Gorov stirred on his couch and opened one eye as Limmar Ponyets entered the heavily reinforced door.</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Ponyets" target="Eskel Gorov" id="1">
      <data key="d12">FRIENDS_WITH</data>
      <data key="d13">0.8</data>
      <data key="d14">we've worked together before and the Board knows it.</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Ponyets" target="Board of Trade" id="0">
      <data key="d12">WORKS_FOR</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">my sales route, as known to the Board of Trade, carries me within fifty parsecs of the system</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Ponyets" target="Gorov" id="0">
      <data key="d12">KNOWS</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">Ponyets indicated the ornamented bracelet that hugged his wrist and Gorov relaxed.</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Ponyets" target="Gorov" id="1">
      <data key="d12">FRIENDS_WITH</data>
      <data key="d13">0.8</data>
      <data key="d14">You're all right, Ponyets. I'm glad they sent you.</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Ponyets" target="Gorov" id="2">
      <data key="d12">WORKS_FOR</data>
      <data key="d13">0.8</data>
      <data key="d14">"Yes," said Gorov, "it was a good sale. Yet you've certainly got an uncomfortable sales technique."</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Ponyets" target="Pherl" id="0">
      <data key="d12">ENEMY_OF</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">Ponyets had met him once already and marked him immediately as prime enemy</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Ponyets" target="Pherl" id="1">
      <data key="d12">KNOWS</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">Pherl laughed, and Ponyets grew red.</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Ponyets" target="Grand Master" id="0">
      <data key="d12">ENEMY_OF</data>
      <data key="d13">0.8</data>
      <data key="d14">prime enemy, and, as a consequence, prime victim.</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Ponyets" target="Grand Master" id="1">
      <data key="d12">KNOWS</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">Ponyets said, "You are wisdom, itself, your Veneration.</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Ponyets" target="small device" id="0">
      <data key="d12">CREATED</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">"This," said Ponyets, stepping back, "is a small device I have constructed myself."</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Ponyets" target="transmutation" id="0">
      <data key="d12">PARTICIPATES_IN</data>
      <data key="d13">0.8</data>
      <data key="d14">"With this machine," began Ponyets, as his hand dropped softly onto the central chamber and caressed its hard, round flanks, "I can turn the iron you discard into gold of the finest quality."</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Ponyets" target="machine" id="0">
      <data key="d12">LOVES</data>
      <data key="d13">0.7</data>
      <data key="d14">as his hand dropped softly onto the central chamber and caressed its hard, round flanks</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Ponyets" target="Foundation series" id="0">
      <data key="d12">MENTIONED_IN</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">Ponyets picked them up.</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Ponyets" target="meeting with Pherl" id="0">
      <data key="d12">PARTICIPATES_IN</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">Another week rubbed away before the meeting with Pherl was arranged.</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Ponyets" target="transmuter" id="0">
      <data key="d12">CREATED</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">"I juiced it up out of a food irradiation chamber."</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Ponyets" target="transmuter" id="1">
      <data key="d12">OWNS</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">when I set up the transmuter for him in my whipped-dog fashion, I incorporated the recorder into the device</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Ponyets" target="Askonians system journey" id="0">
      <data key="d12">PARTICIPATES_IN</data>
      <data key="d13">0.8</data>
      <data key="d14">Then, as on the journey into the Askonian system, so on the journey out, the cylinder of sleek little ships ushered them on their way.</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Ponyets" target="sale" id="0">
      <data key="d12">PARTICIPATES_IN</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">look at what follows from my sale</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Ponyets" target="microfilm-recorder" id="0">
      <data key="d12">CREATED</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">Pherl had never heard nor conceived of a microfilm-recorder.</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Askone" target="Galaxy" id="0">
      <data key="d12">LOCATED_IN</data>
      <data key="d13">0.7</data>
      <data key="d14">"He mumbled strong expressions at that part of the misty lens-form that was the body of the Galaxy."</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Askone" target="extreme borders" id="0">
      <data key="d12">LOCATED_IN</data>
      <data key="d13">0.8</data>
      <data key="d14">Askone, at the extreme borders</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Askone" target="LOCATION" id="0">
      <data key="d12">LOCATED_IN</data>
      <data key="d13">0.8</data>
      <data key="d14">your devil's machines are not wanted anywhere in Askone</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Askone" target="The Foundation" id="0">
      <data key="d12">ENEMY_OF</data>
      <data key="d13">0.8</data>
      <data key="d14">"And can therefore become a focal point for independence and hostility. Yes."</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Askone" target="mining estates" id="0">
      <data key="d12">LOCATED_IN</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">To his mining estates on the outskirts of Askone</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Askone" target="Foundation's system" id="0">
      <data key="d12">MEMBER_OF</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">Askone is now an integral member of the Foundation's system</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Eskel Gorov" target="prison" id="0">
      <data key="d12">PARTICIPATES_IN</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">Eskel Gorov was on Askone – and in prison as well</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Eskel Gorov" target="The Foundation" id="0">
      <data key="d12">MEMBER_OF</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">Master Trader Eskel Gorov was not a trader at all; but that entirely different thing, an agent of the Foundation</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Eskel Gorov" target="Askonians" id="0">
      <data key="d12">PRISONER_OF</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">Eskel Gorov was a prisoner in their hands</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Eskel Gorov" target="Board of Trade" id="0">
      <data key="d12">MEMBER_OF</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">we've worked together before and the Board knows it.</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Askonians" target="The Foundation" id="0">
      <data key="d12">MENTIONED_IN</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">I have heard that the Foundation is rich.</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Grand Master" target="Askonians" id="0">
      <data key="d12">LEADS</data>
      <data key="d13">0.8</data>
      <data key="d14">the Grand Master was on the other side of the Guard-flanked gilded door</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Grand Master" target="Askone" id="0">
      <data key="d12">LEADS</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">snapped the Grand Master</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Grand Master" target="gold" id="0">
      <data key="d12">LOVES</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">Nothing will happen to me as long as the Grand Master has the scent of gold in his nose.</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Grand Master" target="The Foundation" id="0">
      <data key="d12">ENEMY_OF</data>
      <data key="d13">0.8</data>
      <data key="d14">"The Grand Master implied as much."</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Grand Master" target="EVENT" id="0">
      <data key="d12">MENTIONED_IN</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">"A show!" said the Grand Master, grimly.</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Grand Master" target="Foundation series" id="0">
      <data key="d12">MENTIONED_IN</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">The Grand Master seemed coldly amused.</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Grand Master" target="Ponyets" id="0">
      <data key="d12">ENEMY_OF</data>
      <data key="d13">0.8</data>
      <data key="d14">The Grand Master's expression was stony. He did not budge.</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Grand Master" target="council" id="0">
      <data key="d12">LEADS</data>
      <data key="d13">0.8</data>
      <data key="d14">And when the Grand Master rose to his feet to search out disapproval, not a man in the council failed to signal his agreement.</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="traders" target="Guild" id="0">
      <data key="d12">MEMBER_OF</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">contrary to the strictest regulations of our Guild</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Glyptal IV" target="LOCATION" id="0">
      <data key="d12">LOCATED_IN</data>
      <data key="d13">0.8</data>
      <data key="d14">Your people on Glyptal IV have been bombarding me with pleas</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Gorov" target="Grand Master" id="0">
      <data key="d12">ENEMY_OF</data>
      <data key="d13">0.8</data>
      <data key="d14">And he also threatened death by gas.</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Gorov" target="assignment to sell nucleics to Askone" id="0">
      <data key="d12">PARTICIPATES_IN</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">"It's my assignment to sell nucleics to Askone."</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Gorov" target="Empire" id="0">
      <data key="d12">PARTICIPATES_IN</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">Those ships are holdovers of the Empire, no doubt.</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Gorov" target="The Foundation" id="0">
      <data key="d12">WORKS_FOR</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">they send you for that purpose, while I'm only here to ransom you and leave, while you keep on trying?</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Gorov" target="release" id="0">
      <data key="d12">PARTICIPATES_IN</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">Gorov was released on the thirtieth day</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Gorov" target="ship" id="0">
      <data key="d12">OWNS</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">the quarantined and untouched abomination that was his ship.</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Gorov" target="Askonians system journey" id="0">
      <data key="d12">PARTICIPATES_IN</data>
      <data key="d13">0.8</data>
      <data key="d14">Then, as on the journey into the Askonian system, so on the journey out, the cylinder of sleek little ships ushered them on their way.</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Gorov" target="Ponyets" id="0">
      <data key="d12">KNOWS</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">Gorov was evidently lost. He said, weakly, "Do you mind explaining'?" "What's there to explain? It's obvious, Gorov.</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Pherl" target="Grand Master" id="0">
      <data key="d12">KNOWS</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">Pherl whispered urgently into his ruler's ear.</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Pherl" target="Grand Master" id="1">
      <data key="d12">ENEMY_OF</data>
      <data key="d13">0.8</data>
      <data key="d14">young and newly-advanced a favorite of the Grand Master is bound to make powerful enemies among the great ones of the State</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Pherl" target="Ponyets" id="0">
      <data key="d12">ENEMY_OF</data>
      <data key="d13">0.8</data>
      <data key="d14">the thin-faced Pherl was roused to open speech. "Your Veneration, the gold is from a poisoned source."</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Pherl" target="Ponyets" id="1">
      <data key="d12">KNOWS</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">Pherl said gloomily, "So it would seem.</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Pherl" target="suburban villa" id="0">
      <data key="d12">LOCATED_IN</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">He was in Pherl's suburban villa under guard.</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Pherl" target="council" id="0">
      <data key="d12">MEMBER_OF</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">you are young-very young for a member of the council</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Pherl" target="Five Tribes" id="0">
      <data key="d12">FAMILY_OF</data>
      <data key="d13">0.8</data>
      <data key="d14">there are those that say you are not a member of one of the Five Tribes</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Pherl" target="Foundation series" id="0">
      <data key="d12">MENTIONED_IN</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">And now Pherl stiffened</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Pherl" target="election" id="0">
      <data key="d12">PARTICIPATES_IN</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">The transmuter gets him an election</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Pherl" target="mining estates" id="0">
      <data key="d12">OWNS</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">To his mining estates on the outskirts of Askone</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Pherl" target="private navy" id="0">
      <data key="d12">MEMBER_OF</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">That's Pherl's private navy escorting us</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Pherl" target="capital crime in Askone" id="0">
      <data key="d12">PARTICIPATES_IN</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">He took the transmuter. That was a capital crime in Askone.</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Randel" target="Foundation series" id="0">
      <data key="d12">MENTIONED_IN</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">Randel, your buckles.</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="transmuter" target="dungeon" id="0">
      <data key="d12">LOCATED_IN</data>
      <data key="d13">0.7</data>
      <data key="d14">You may bury the transmuter in the deepest dungeon</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Askonian system" target="journey" id="0">
      <data key="d12">LOCATED_IN</data>
      <data key="d13">0.7</data>
      <data key="d14">Then, as on the journey into the Askonian system, so on the journey out</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Hober Mallow" target="Merchant Princes" id="0">
      <data key="d12">MEMBER_OF</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">It is never forgotten that he ended it as the first of the Merchant Princes</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Hober Mallow" target="The Foundation" id="0">
      <data key="d12">WORKS_FOR</data>
      <data key="d13">0.8</data>
      <data key="d14">economic control of the Foundation grew. The traders grew rich; and with riches came power.... It is sometimes forgotten that Hober Mallow began life as an ordinary trader.</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Hober Mallow" target="The Foundation" id="1">
      <data key="d12">MEMBER_OF</data>
      <data key="d13">0.8</data>
      <data key="d14">If, before the two months are up, the Foundation locates you, the microfilm is my report of the trip.</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Hober Mallow" target="The Foundation" id="2">
      <data key="d12">LEADS</data>
      <data key="d13">0.8</data>
      <data key="d14">And there isn't a factory, not a trading center. not a shipping line that isn't under my control</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Hober Mallow" target="Smyrno" id="0">
      <data key="d12">LOCATED_IN</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">Hober Mallow of Smyrno, Master Trader, smoked quietly, almost indifferently.</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Hober Mallow" target="Jaim Twer" id="0">
      <data key="d12">KNOWS</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">Hober Mallow kept a second appointment. He had listened long, and now he said cautiously, "Yes, I've heard of your campaigns to get trader representation in the council. But why me, Twer?" Jaim Twer, who would remind you any time, asked or unasked, that he was in the first group of Outlanders to receive a lay education at the Foundation, beamed.</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Hober Mallow" target="Jaim Twer" id="1">
      <data key="d12">ENEMY_OF</data>
      <data key="d13">0.8</data>
      <data key="d14">A known enemy is relatively safe. I invited Twer to come with me.</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Hober Mallow" target="Trader's Convention" id="0">
      <data key="d12">PARTICIPATES_IN</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">"Remember when I met you first, last year." "At the Trader's Convention." "Right. You ran the meeting.</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Hober Mallow" target="trading" id="0">
      <data key="d12">PARTICIPATES_IN</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">Hober Mallow said thoughtfully, "Good trading material here."</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Hober Mallow" target="Far Star" id="0">
      <data key="d12">WORKS_FOR</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">Hober Mallow, in his private quarters with Senior Lieutenant Drawt, handed him an envelope, a roll of microfilm, and a silvery spheroid. "As of an hour from now, Lieutenant, you're Acting Captain of the Far Star, until I return, –or forever."</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Hober Mallow" target="Far Star" id="1">
      <data key="d12">LEADS</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">"As of an hour from now, Lieutenant, you're Acting Captain of the Far Star, until I return, –or forever."</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Hober Mallow" target="a far province" id="0">
      <data key="d12">LOCATED_IN</data>
      <data key="d13">0.8</data>
      <data key="d14">I come from a far province</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Hober Mallow" target="trial" id="0">
      <data key="d12">PARTICIPATES_IN</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">the fourth day of the trial of Hober Mallow, Master Trader</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Hober Mallow" target="proceedings" id="0">
      <data key="d12">PARTICIPATES_IN</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">Hober Mallow stepped through a hostile whisper to the empty space before the mayor's bench.</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Hober Mallow" target="mayoralty" id="0">
      <data key="d12">WORKS_FOR</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">Two years of the mayoralty had made him a bit more housebroken, a bit softer, a bit more patient, –but it had not made him learn to like government reports and the mind-breaking officialese in which they were written.</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Hober Mallow" target="Jorane Sutt" id="0">
      <data key="d12">ENEMY_OF</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">Jorane Sutt's face congested with blood in a sudden access of emotion. "And I warn you, Hober Mallow of Smyrno, that if you arrest me, there will be no quarter."</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Hober Mallow" target="Sutt" id="0">
      <data key="d12">HATES</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">Galaxy, he hates me.</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Hober Mallow" target="Jael" id="0">
      <data key="d12">KNOWS</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">Mallow looked up, grim in his turn, "Once and for all, Jael, there is no possibility of a popular rebellion."</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Hober Mallow" target="Foundation series" id="0">
      <data key="d12">MENTIONED_IN</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">Hober Mallow took his place next to Hari Seldon and Salvor Hardin in the hearts of the people of the Foundation.</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Hober Mallow" target="KORELL" id="0">
      <data key="d12">MENTIONED_IN</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">Hober Mallow took his place next to Hari Seldon and Salvor Hardin in the hearts of the people of the Foundation.</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Jorane Sutt" target="Hari Seldon" id="0">
      <data key="d12">MENTIONED_IN</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">Jorane Sutt put the tips of carefully-manicured fingers together and said, "It's something of a puzzle. In fact – and this is in the strictest of confidence – it may be another one of Hari Seldon's crises."</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Jorane Sutt" target="mayor" id="0">
      <data key="d12">WORKS_FOR</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">As secretary to the mayor</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Jorane Sutt" target="The Foundation" id="0">
      <data key="d12">MENTIONED_IN</data>
      <data key="d13">0.8</data>
      <data key="d14">The Foundation's greatest asset throughout the Periphery is its reputation of power.</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Jorane Sutt" target="The Foundation" id="1">
      <data key="d12">MEMBER_OF</data>
      <data key="d13">0.7</data>
      <data key="d14">They've been inciting the priesthood of the outer planets to take sides in the factional quarrels of the Foundation.</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Jorane Sutt" target="cabinet" id="0">
      <data key="d12">LEADS</data>
      <data key="d13">0.8</data>
      <data key="d14">you were booted out of your cabinet seat by Jorane Sutt</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Jorane Sutt" target="the mayor" id="0">
      <data key="d12">WORKS_FOR</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">the secretary to the mayor</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Jorane Sutt" target="Mallow" id="0">
      <data key="d12">ENEMY_OF</data>
      <data key="d13">0.8</data>
      <data key="d14">He didn't trust me. Perhaps he thought I was selling nuclear power to enemies and plotting rebellion.</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Jorane Sutt" target="Mallow" id="1">
      <data key="d12">KNOWS</data>
      <data key="d13">0.8</data>
      <data key="d14">Jorane Sutt shook his head coldly at the nervous high priest, while his eyes blazed fixedly on Mallow's face.</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Jorane Sutt" target="Foundation series" id="0">
      <data key="d12">MENTIONED_IN</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">Would Jorane Sutt and Publis Manlio have had me fall into a stupid, odious trap</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Jorane Sutt" target="Hober Mallow" id="0">
      <data key="d12">ENEMY_OF</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">Jorane Sutt's face congested with blood in a sudden access of emotion. "And I warn you, Hober Mallow of Smyrno, that if you arrest me, there will be no quarter."</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Korellian Republic" target="Argo family" id="0">
      <data key="d12">LOCATED_IN</data>
      <data key="d13">0.8</data>
      <data key="d14">That," he said quietly, "is the Korellian Republic." The trader nodded, "I've been there. Stinking rathole! I suppose you can call it a republic but it's always someone out of the Argo family that gets elected Commdor each time.</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Korell" target="Republic" id="0">
      <data key="d12">LOCATED_IN</data>
      <data key="d13">0.8</data>
      <data key="d14">within the territory of the Republic</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Korell" target="The Foundation" id="0">
      <data key="d12">ENEMY_OF</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">You are here against the law of both Korell and the Foundation.</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Korell" target="The Foundation" id="1">
      <data key="d12">LOCATED_IN</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">He was here against the laws of Korell and the Foundation.</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Korell" target="passage" id="0">
      <data key="d12">MENTIONED_IN</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">Korell is that frequent phenomenon in history: the republic whose ruler has every attribute of the absolute monarch but the name.</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Korell" target="shipyards" id="0">
      <data key="d12">LOCATED_IN</data>
      <data key="d13">0.7</data>
      <data key="d14">You'd find it in the shipyards and the steel foundries only.</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Korell" target="steel foundries" id="0">
      <data key="d12">LOCATED_IN</data>
      <data key="d13">0.7</data>
      <data key="d14">You'd find it in the shipyards and the steel foundries only.</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Korell" target="us" id="0">
      <data key="d12">ENEMY_OF</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">Korell is now at war with us.</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Korell" target="Empire" id="0">
      <data key="d12">LOCATED_IN</data>
      <data key="d13">0.7</data>
      <data key="d14">But it was only after my visit to the Empire that I first realized exactly what a weapon I could build that trade into.</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Korell" target="Foundation series" id="0">
      <data key="d12">LOCATION</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">the industrialists of Korell</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Korell" target="Galaxy" id="0">
      <data key="d12">LOCATED_IN</data>
      <data key="d13">0.8</data>
      <data key="d14">in whole sectors of the Galaxy</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Mallow" target="Smyrno" id="0">
      <data key="d12">BORN_IN</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">You're a Smyrnian – born in Smyrno</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Mallow" target="Smyrno" id="1">
      <data key="d12">FROM</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">You're from Smyrno, aren't you?</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Mallow" target="The Foundation" id="0">
      <data key="d12">WORKS_FOR</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">You're a Foundation man by education only.</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Mallow" target="The Foundation" id="1">
      <data key="d12">PARTICIPATES_IN</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">It's another to fool around with an accredited envoy of the Foundation</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Mallow" target="Outlanders" id="0">
      <data key="d12">KNOWS</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">You know the Outlanders.</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Mallow" target="Korellian Republic" id="0">
      <data key="d12">KNOWS</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">you've been to Korell and you know the Korellians</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Mallow" target="Korellian Republic" id="1">
      <data key="d12">ENEMY_OF</data>
      <data key="d13">0.7</data>
      <data key="d14">You know that these Korellians kill captured missionaries.</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Mallow" target="Twer" id="0">
      <data key="d12">KNOWS</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">Mallow's hand fell on the other's balled fist.</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Mallow" target="trip" id="0">
      <data key="d12">PARTICIPATES_IN</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">"It'll be my first trip in three years." Mallow grasped and shook the other's hand, "Good! All fired good! And now I've got to round up the boys."</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Mallow" target="crew of a master trader" id="0">
      <data key="d12">LEADS</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">it was in speed above all that the crew of a master trader excelled. Mallow entered slowly</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Mallow" target="Lieutenant Tinter" id="0">
      <data key="d12">KNOWS</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">His eye slid to Lieutenant Tinter, who shifted uneasily</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Mallow" target="Watch-Sergeant Demen" id="0">
      <data key="d12">KNOWS</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">and to Watch-Sergeant Demen, whose blank face and stolid figure flanked the other.</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Mallow" target="ORGANIZATION" id="0">
      <data key="d12">WORKS_FOR</data>
      <data key="d13">0.8</data>
      <data key="d14">Mallow said quietly, "First, who let this man in without orders from me?"</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Mallow" target="sergeant" id="0">
      <data key="d12">LEADS</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">Mallow cut him short, "I sympathize with your feelings, sergeant, and understand them."</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Mallow" target="Korellian mob" id="0">
      <data key="d12">ENEMY_OF</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">Enemy units! Several thousands of them in the persons of the individual members of a Korellian mob.</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Mallow" target="EVENT" id="0">
      <data key="d12">PARTICIPATES_IN</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">Mallow passed from one to the other through an underground passage, and found himself in the silent, ozone-tinged atmosphere of the powerhouse.</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Mallow" target="EVENT" id="1">
      <data key="d12">MENTIONED_IN</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">Mallow, the real Mallow of the present, took up the burden of his narration</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Mallow" target="ship" id="0">
      <data key="d12">LEADS</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">there's nothing short of tyranny that can run my ship the way I want it run.</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Mallow" target="governor" id="0">
      <data key="d12">KNOWS</data>
      <data key="d13">0.7</data>
      <data key="d14">That wobbly-kneed governor or whatever-he-was can't save him.</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Mallow" target="test" id="0">
      <data key="d12">PARTICIPATES_IN</data>
      <data key="d13">0.7</data>
      <data key="d14">I think we passed a test.</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Mallow" target="Commdor of Korell" id="0">
      <data key="d12">KNOWS</data>
      <data key="d13">0.8</data>
      <data key="d14">It is fortunate that I have you to deal with then, Commdor.</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Mallow" target="Commdor of Korell" id="1">
      <data key="d12">BRIBED</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">A bribed the Commdor with the trinkets and gadgets that form the trader's usual stock.</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Mallow" target="Master Trader" id="0">
      <data key="d12">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">I'm a Master Trader.</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Mallow" target="Master Trader" id="1">
      <data key="d12">MEMBER_OF</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">I'm a Master Trader</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Mallow" target="Foundation series" id="0">
      <data key="d12">MENTIONED_IN</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">Mallow snapped the chain about the girl's waist</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Mallow" target="necklace" id="0">
      <data key="d12">OWNS</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">Mallow handed her a necklace of dull pebbles</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Mallow" target="belt" id="0">
      <data key="d12">OWNS</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">Mallow snapped the chain about the girl's waist</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Mallow" target="meeting" id="0">
      <data key="d12">PARTICIPATES_IN</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">it was the Commdor who set the terms of the meeting, and not myself.</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Mallow" target="foundry" id="0">
      <data key="d12">PARTICIPATES_IN</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">it played unaccustomed host to the Commdor and his court.</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Mallow" target="demonstration" id="0">
      <data key="d12">PARTICIPATES_IN</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">Mallow punched clean, beautiful round holes through an inch of hard steel at every touch of his nuclear drill. "Just one more demonstration."</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Mallow" target="directions to the center of government" id="0">
      <data key="d12">MENTIONED_IN</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">All I need are the directions to the center of government.</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Mallow" target="trader" id="0">
      <data key="d12">WORKS_FOR</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">I'm a trader out there</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Mallow" target="fighting" id="0">
      <data key="d12">PARTICIPATES_IN</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">Fighting and scars are part of a trader's overhead</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Mallow" target="rim of the Galaxy" id="0">
      <data key="d12">LOCATED_IN</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">I'm a trader out there – out toward the rim of the Galaxy</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Mallow" target="Barr" id="0">
      <data key="d12">KNOWS</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">Mallow sat silent, and waited. Then, "What of your sixth son?" he asked softly.</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Mallow" target="Barr" id="1">
      <data key="d12">FRIENDS_WITH</data>
      <data key="d13">0.7</data>
      <data key="d14">He returned but once, for a moment, to the old patrician's house, before leaving it entirely, however.</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Mallow" target="old man" id="0">
      <data key="d12">KNOWS</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">"I knew you when you entered."</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Mallow" target="journey to the city" id="0">
      <data key="d12">PARTICIPATES_IN</data>
      <data key="d13">0.8</data>
      <data key="d14">Now I'll tell you how to get to the city–" Five minutes later, Mallow was gone.</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Mallow" target="provisions" id="0">
      <data key="d12">OWNS</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">And when Onum Barr stepped into his little garden early the next morning, he found a box at his feet. It contained provisions, concentrated provisions such as one would find aboard ship, and alien in taste and preparation.</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Mallow" target="tech-man's guild" id="0">
      <data key="d12">PARTICIPATES_IN</data>
      <data key="d13">0.8</data>
      <data key="d14">the privileges and protections of the tech-man's guild.</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Mallow" target="the display" id="0">
      <data key="d12">PARTICIPATES_IN</data>
      <data key="d13">0.7</data>
      <data key="d14">but the display will take only three seconds.</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Mallow" target="tech-man" id="0">
      <data key="d12">KNOWS</data>
      <data key="d13">0.8</data>
      <data key="d14">following Mallow's gesture</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Mallow" target="council seat" id="0">
      <data key="d12">LOVES</data>
      <data key="d13">0.8</data>
      <data key="d14">I'd rather rest in a council seat.</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Mallow" target="Jael" id="0">
      <data key="d12">KNOWS</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">The man beside him placed a cigar between Mallow's teeth and lit it.</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Mallow" target="Jael" id="1">
      <data key="d12">WORKS_FOR</data>
      <data key="d13">0.7</data>
      <data key="d14">Mind if Jael stays? He wants a compromise earnestly. He can act as mediator if tempers rise.</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Mallow" target="Jorane Sutt" id="0">
      <data key="d12">ENEMY_OF</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">Jorane Sutt, the same fellow who'd rather lose an eyeball than see me in the council.</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Mallow" target="Jorane Sutt" id="1">
      <data key="d12">MEETING_WITH</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">the day of my meeting with Jorane Sutt and Jaim Twer</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Mallow" target="Jaim Twer" id="0">
      <data key="d12">FRIENDS_WITH</data>
      <data key="d13">0.7</data>
      <data key="d14">Now, how about your own man – this Jaim Twer?</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Mallow" target="Jaim Twer" id="1">
      <data key="d12">KNOWS</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">Jaim Twer was his man from the beginning, though neither of them knew that I knew that.</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Mallow" target="Jaim Twer" id="2">
      <data key="d12">MEETING_WITH</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">the day of my meeting with Jorane Sutt and Jaim Twer</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Mallow" target="Sutt" id="0">
      <data key="d12">KNOWS</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">Mallow fastened his belt and said, "Take your choice of chairs, Sutt."</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Mallow" target="Sutt" id="1">
      <data key="d12">HATES</data>
      <data key="d13">0.8</data>
      <data key="d14">The event struck me at the moment as a move by Sutt, and passed beyond my comprehension or calculation.</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Mallow" target="Sutt" id="2">
      <data key="d12">ENEMY_OF</data>
      <data key="d13">0.8</data>
      <data key="d14">Neither detected any change in the other, except for that subtle atmosphere about each which made it quite evident that the roles of ruler and defier had changed.</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Mallow" target="Korell" id="0">
      <data key="d12">PARTICIPATES_IN</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">what, for instance, did you do at Korell?</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Mallow" target="Korell" id="1">
      <data key="d12">TRADED_WITH</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">you traded with Korell to their exclusive benefit for three years.</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Mallow" target="Korell" id="2">
      <data key="d12">VISITED</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">When I first landed on Korell</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Mallow" target="palace" id="0">
      <data key="d12">OWNS</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">and there's this palace you have</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Mallow" target="Foundation society" id="0">
      <data key="d12">MEMBER_OF</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">a very considerable and expensive swathe – through the upper layers of Foundation society.</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Mallow" target="trade" id="0">
      <data key="d12">PARTICIPATES_IN</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">your attempt at trade for its own sake</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Mallow" target="foreign spiritual power" id="0">
      <data key="d12">HATES</data>
      <data key="d13">0.8</data>
      <data key="d14">an insecure overlordship, based on the hated supremacy of a foreign spiritual power</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Mallow" target="Foundation versus Hober Mallow, Master Trader" id="0">
      <data key="d12">PARTICIPATES_IN</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">the case of the Foundation versus Hober Mallow, Master Trader, is begun.</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Mallow" target="council" id="0">
      <data key="d12">PARTICIPATES_IN</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">Mallow cleared his throat theatrically, and continued:</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Mallow" target="Far Star" id="0">
      <data key="d12">WORKS_FOR</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">The officers of the Far Star struck their stiff, impossible attitudes. A gun pointed from Mallow's rigid hand.</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Mallow" target="mob" id="0">
      <data key="d12">LEADS</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">I control the mob, –for today, at any rate.</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Mallow" target="Seldon Crisis" id="0">
      <data key="d12">PARTICIPATES_IN</data>
      <data key="d13">0.8</data>
      <data key="d14">There's still that Seldon crisis coming up, and when it comes I have to be mayor and high priest.</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Mallow" target="Ankor Jael" id="0">
      <data key="d12">KNOWS</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">Ankor Jael blinked at Mallow out of a haggard face.</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Mallow" target="mayor and high priest" id="0">
      <data key="d12">WANTS_TO_BE</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">That's why I must be mayor and high priest</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Mallow" target="Minister of Education and Propaganda" id="0">
      <data key="d12">WORKS_FOR</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">What did I make you Minister of Education and Propaganda for?</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Mallow" target="speech" id="0">
      <data key="d12">PARTICIPATES_IN</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">And your speech last night just about handed the election to Sutt with a smile and a pat.</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Mallow" target="Empire" id="0">
      <data key="d12">ENEMY_OF</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">And if you beat Korell, what of the Empire? That is the real enemy.</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Mallow" target="Siwenna" id="0">
      <data key="d12">VISITED</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">your records of your visit to Siwenna were complete</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Publis Manlio" target="The Foundation" id="0">
      <data key="d12">WORKS_FOR</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">two great offices of the Foundation. He was Foreign Secretary in the mayor's cabinet</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Publis Manlio" target="The Foundation" id="1">
      <data key="d12">MEMBER_OF</data>
      <data key="d13">0.7</data>
      <data key="d14">They've been inciting the priesthood of the outer planets to take sides in the factional quarrels of the Foundation.</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Publis Manlio" target="Church" id="0">
      <data key="d12">LEADS</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">he was, in addition, Primate of the Church</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Publis Manlio" target="Church" id="1">
      <data key="d12">WORKS_FOR</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">As High Priest and Primate of the Church, he rouses the fanatic hordes–</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Publis Manlio" target="Hierarchy" id="0">
      <data key="d12">MEMBER_OF</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">Publis Manlio's men on the outer planets–</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Publis Manlio" target="Foundation series" id="0">
      <data key="d12">MENTIONED_IN</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">Would Jorane Sutt and Publis Manlio have had me fall into a stupid, odious trap</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Manlio" target="crisis" id="0">
      <data key="d12">PARTICIPATES_IN</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">"And you've made your plans to meet this crisis?" Sutt nodded. "And I," continued Manlio, "am to play a part in it?" Sutt nodded again</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Manlio" target="Seldon Crisis" id="0">
      <data key="d12">PARTICIPATES_IN</data>
      <data key="d13">0.7</data>
      <data key="d14">"The cure must come quickly, before the Seldon Crisis becomes acute."</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Jaim Twer" target="Outlanders" id="0">
      <data key="d12">MEMBER_OF</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">Jaim Twer, who would remind you any time, asked or unasked, that he was in the first group of Outlanders to receive a lay education at the Foundation, beamed.</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Jaim Twer" target="The Foundation" id="0">
      <data key="d12">MENTIONED_IN</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">Jaim Twer, who would remind you any time, asked or unasked, that he was in the first group of Outlanders to receive a lay education at the Foundation, beamed.</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Jaim Twer" target="solitaire" id="0">
      <data key="d12">PARTICIPATES_IN</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">Jaim Twer itched and fretted over a game of solitaire.</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Jaim Twer" target="Hober Mallow" id="0">
      <data key="d12">KNOWS</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">Jaim Twer fidgeted and shuffled his feet. He said, "What's twisting your face?" Hober Mallow lifted out of his brooding, "Is my face twisted? It's not meant so."</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Jaim Twer" target="political party of the traders" id="0">
      <data key="d12">PARTICIPATES_IN</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">for the three years he had pretended to head a political party of the traders</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Jaim Twer" target="holy orders" id="0">
      <data key="d12">MEMBER_OF</data>
      <data key="d13">0.8</data>
      <data key="d14">I knew then that he was in holy orders and perhaps a full-fledged priest</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Jaim Twer" target="Jorane Sutt" id="0">
      <data key="d12">BOUGHT_BY</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">he had been a bought man of Jorane Sutt</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Jaim Twer" target="Jorane Sutt" id="1">
      <data key="d12">WORKS_FOR</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">he had been a bought man of Jorane Sutt</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Jaim Twer" target="EVENT" id="0">
      <data key="d12">MENTIONED_IN</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">Jaim Twer's emotions through the whole business shows clearly a priestly education</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Twer" target="trip" id="0">
      <data key="d12">PARTICIPATES_IN</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">"All right. I'll go." He held out his hand, "It'll be my first trip in three years."</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Twer" target="Mallow" id="0">
      <data key="d12">KNOWS</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">Twer broke in, "Why the punishment, Mallow?"</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Twer" target="Mallow" id="1">
      <data key="d12">ENEMY_OF</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">A known enemy is relatively safe.</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Twer" target="Mallow" id="2">
      <data key="d12">SPY</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">He is a spy, performing his paid job.</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Twer" target="EVENT" id="0">
      <data key="d12">PARTICIPATES_IN</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">Twer bringing up the rear. The conversation played itself out, word for word.</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Twer" target="The Foundation" id="0">
      <data key="d12">MEMBER_OF</data>
      <data key="d13">0.7</data>
      <data key="d14">Your three years in politics seem to have gotten you out of trader habits.</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Twer" target="foundry" id="0">
      <data key="d12">PARTICIPATES_IN</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">He had taken the instrument held out to him by Twer</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Twer" target="council" id="0">
      <data key="d12">PARTICIPATES_IN</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">I invited Twer to come with me. He accepted.</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Far Star" target="docks" id="0">
      <data key="d12">LOCATED_IN</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">You know where the Far Star docks, don't you?</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Far Star" target="Korell" id="0">
      <data key="d12">LOCATED_IN</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">The spaceport itself was decrepit and decayed, and the crew of the Far Star were drearily aware of that.</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Far Star" target="The Foundation" id="0">
      <data key="d12">MENTIONED_IN</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">And behind you is there not the Foundation? And above and all-about you is there not the Spirit that rules the universe?" He paused for breath. And then the great outer voice of the Far Star ceased</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Far Star" target="Terminus" id="0">
      <data key="d12">LOCATED_IN</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">the Far Star waited to return with him to the planet, Terminus.</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Commdor Asper Argo" target="Korell" id="0">
      <data key="d12">LEADS</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">in the fierce determination of its ruler, the Commdor Asper Argo, with his strict regulation of the traders and his stricter prohibition of the missionaries</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Commdor Asper Argo" target="demonstration" id="0">
      <data key="d12">MENTIONED_IN</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">Commdor Asper fingered scraps of steel.</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Commdor Asper Argo" target="bodyguard" id="0">
      <data key="d12">LEADS</data>
      <data key="d13">0.8</data>
      <data key="d14">The Commdor's own bodyguard, in the confusion, had struggled to the front line</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Lieutenant Tinter" target="Mallow" id="0">
      <data key="d12">KNOWS</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">Lieutenant Tinter was back, troubled. "Speak!" said Mallow, shortly.</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="sergeant" target="ORGANIZATION" id="0">
      <data key="d12">MEMBER_OF</data>
      <data key="d13">0.8</data>
      <data key="d14">The watch sergeant stepped forward.</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Enemy units" target="Mallow" id="0">
      <data key="d12">ENEMY_OF</data>
      <data key="d13">0.8</data>
      <data key="d14">Enemy units in sight! Instruction desired!</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Tinter" target="Mallow" id="0">
      <data key="d12">WORKS_FOR</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">"Tinter!" The trader never turned, but the back of his neck was red. "Get the outer speaker working and find out what they want.</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Revered Parma" target="The Foundation" id="0">
      <data key="d12">MEMBER_OF</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">"You! Revered Parma! Did you know that, by convention, no Foundation missionaries may enter the Korellian territory?"</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Revered Parma" target="incident" id="0">
      <data key="d12">PARTICIPATES_IN</data>
      <data key="d13">0.8</data>
      <data key="d14">Our friend, Revered Parma, was considerably confused. He seemed at no time to be in complete possession of his wits.</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Trader Mallow" target="official communication" id="0">
      <data key="d12">MENTIONED_IN</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">"Sir, official communication received." "Submit immediately!"</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Commdor of Korell" target="state" id="0">
      <data key="d12">LEADS</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">since I succeeded my illustrious father to the leadership of the state</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Commdor of Korell" target="Peace" id="0">
      <data key="d12">LOVES</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">I don't think there is anyone in the Periphery who has so near his heart the ideal of Peace, as I have.</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Commdor of Korell" target="his people" id="0">
      <data key="d12">LEADS</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">the despots and monarchs of surrounding worlds, which haven't the benefit of enlightened administration, often lack the qualities that would make a ruler well-beloved.</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Commdor of Korell" target="people" id="0">
      <data key="d12">LOVES</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">The true wealth is the love of one's people. I have that.</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Commdor of Korell" target="house" id="0">
      <data key="d12">LOCATED_IN</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">The Commdor referred to his dwelling place as a house.</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Commdor of Korell" target="Commdora" id="0">
      <data key="d12">FAMILY_OF</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">This is one of the Commdora's girls.</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Commdor of Korell" target="Foundation series" id="0">
      <data key="d12">MENTIONED_IN</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">The Commdor snuffled</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Commdor of Korell" target="belt" id="0">
      <data key="d12">OWNS</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">It's yours, Commdor</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Commdor of Korell" target="necklace" id="0">
      <data key="d12">OWNS</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">It's yours, Commdor</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Commdor of Korell" target="government" id="0">
      <data key="d12">WORKS_FOR</data>
      <data key="d13">0.8</data>
      <data key="d14">if they're available as a government monopoly at nine hundred percent profit.</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Commdor of Korell" target="Trader Mallow" id="0">
      <data key="d12">KNOWS</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">"It could be arranged, Trader Mallow. But tomorrow, tomorrow. Would you dine with us tonight?"</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Commdor of Korell" target="profits" id="0">
      <data key="d12">LOVES</data>
      <data key="d13">0.8</data>
      <data key="d14">"Commdor," said Mallow, dryly, "I give you my word that religion would cut my profits."</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Commdor of Korell" target="city" id="0">
      <data key="d12">LOCATED_IN</data>
      <data key="d13">0.7</data>
      <data key="d14">"Do you have a steel foundry in this city?"</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Commdor of Korell" target="meeting" id="0">
      <data key="d12">PARTICIPATES_IN</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">it was the Commdor who set the terms of the meeting, and not myself.</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Commdor of Korell" target="foundry" id="0">
      <data key="d12">PARTICIPATES_IN</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">it played unaccustomed host to the Commdor and his court.</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Commdor of Korell" target="rebellion against rebel viceroy" id="0">
      <data key="d12">PARTICIPATES_IN</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">For when the Emperor's Admiral approached the province at the head of a fleet, Siwenna itself rebelled against its rebel viceroy.</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Commdor of Korell" target="treasure-chests" id="0">
      <data key="d12">OWNS</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">It's straight from the treasure-chests of the Commdor of Korell.</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Commdor of Korell" target="Korell" id="0">
      <data key="d12">LOCATED_IN</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">the Commdor of Korell</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Commdor of Korell" target="Korell" id="1">
      <data key="d12">LEADS</data>
      <data key="d13">0.8</data>
      <data key="d14">The Commdor shrugged and turned away.</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Commdor of Korell" target="nuclear blasters" id="0">
      <data key="d12">OWNS</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">nuclear blasters in the possession of the Commdor's private bodyguard</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Commdor of Korell" target="The Foundation" id="0">
      <data key="d12">ENEMY_OF</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">It is over, and there is war between Korell and the Foundation.</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Commdor of Korell" target="Lepold I" id="0">
      <data key="d12">HATES</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">The Commdor waited, and then said to the closed door, with malignance and hate, "And when I am master of what you call the hinterland, I may be sufficiently respectable to do without your father's arrogance and his daughter's tongue. Completely – without!"</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Commdor of Korell" target="daughter" id="0">
      <data key="d12">HATES</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">The Commdor waited, and then said to the closed door, with malignance and hate, "And when I am master of what you call the hinterland, I may be sufficiently respectable to do without your father's arrogance and his daughter's tongue. Completely – without!"</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Asper" target="Commdor of Korell" id="0">
      <data key="d12">KNOWS</data>
      <data key="d13">0.8</data>
      <data key="d14">It is fortunate that I have you to deal with then, Commdor.</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Asper" target="house" id="0">
      <data key="d12">LEADS</data>
      <data key="d13">0.7</data>
      <data key="d14">Just the type of dwelling, Mallow thought sourly, for Asper, the Well-Beloved.</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="house" target="capital" id="0">
      <data key="d12">LOCATED_IN</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">it was built on an eminence that overlooked the capital.</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Commdora" target="Foundation series" id="0">
      <data key="d12">MENTIONED_IN</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">for the Commdora</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Commdora" target="Commdor of Korell" id="0">
      <data key="d12">FAMILY_OF</data>
      <data key="d13">0.8</data>
      <data key="d14">The Commdora laughed shortly</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="young man" target="dinner" id="0">
      <data key="d12">PARTICIPATES_IN</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">young man will attend at dinner tonight</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="young man" target="place" id="0">
      <data key="d12">LOCATED_IN</data>
      <data key="d13">0.8</data>
      <data key="d14">Room will have to be arranged for his men somewhere about the place</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="She" target="barbarians" id="0">
      <data key="d12">ENEMY_OF</data>
      <data key="d13">0.8</data>
      <data key="d14">You are very friendly with these barbarians. Perhaps that is why I was not to be permitted to attend your conversation.</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="She" target="my father" id="0">
      <data key="d12">FAMILY_OF</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">My father would pulverize your toy nation to meteoric dust.</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="bodyguard" target="nuclear weapons" id="0">
      <data key="d12">OWNS</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">The Commdor's own bodyguard, in the confusion, had struggled to the front line, and Mallow, for the first time, was near enough to see their unfamiliar hand-weapons in detail. They were nuclear!</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Onum Barr" target="Siwenna" id="0">
      <data key="d12">LOCATED_IN</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">I am Onum Barr of Siwenna</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Onum Barr" target="Empire" id="0">
      <data key="d12">LEADS</data>
      <data key="d13">0.7</data>
      <data key="d14">once Patrician of the Empire</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Onum Barr" target="provincial senate" id="0">
      <data key="d12">MEMBER_OF</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">I was a patrician and a member of the provincial senate.</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Siwenna" target="Normannic Sector" id="0">
      <data key="d12">LOCATED_IN</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">Siwenna is no longer capital of the Normannic Sector.</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Siwenna" target="provincial capital" id="0">
      <data key="d12">LOCATED_IN</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">When Siwenna was the provincial capital</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Siwenna" target="province" id="0">
      <data key="d12">LOCATED_IN</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">For when the Emperor's Admiral approached the province at the head of a fleet, Siwenna itself rebelled against its rebel viceroy.</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Siwenna" target="knowledge of nucleics" id="0">
      <data key="d12">POSSESSES</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">I know that it possesses the knowledge of nucleics.</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Siwenna" target="Trantor" id="0">
      <data key="d12">LOCATED_IN</data>
      <data key="d13">0.8</data>
      <data key="d14">We have the largest and best on this side of Trantor itself.</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Siwenna" target="Foundation series" id="0">
      <data key="d12">MENTIONED_IN</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">dogs of Siwenna</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Orsha II" target="Normannic Sector" id="0">
      <data key="d12">LOCATED_IN</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">It's on Orsha II. Twenty parsecs off.</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Stannell VI" target="reign" id="0">
      <data key="d12">MENTIONED_IN</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">but for the reign of Stannell VI, and he died fifty years ago.</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Barr" target="lonely life" id="0">
      <data key="d12">MENTIONED_IN</data>
      <data key="d13">0.8</data>
      <data key="d14">Barr wondered if he were growing garrulous. It was a lonely life out here, and he had so little chance to talk to men.</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Barr" target="rebellion" id="0">
      <data key="d12">PARTICIPATES_IN</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">They rebelled; or I should say, we rebelled, for I was one of the minor leaders.</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Barr" target="viceroy" id="0">
      <data key="d12">ENEMY_OF</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">I am his enemy</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Barr" target="son" id="0">
      <data key="d12">FAMILY_OF</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">My son hears tales.</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Barr" target="Foundation series" id="0">
      <data key="d12">MENTIONED_IN</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">replied Barr, decisively.</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Barr" target="city" id="0">
      <data key="d12">LOCATED_IN</data>
      <data key="d13">0.8</data>
      <data key="d14">In the city, where the inhabitants are still called rebels, you would be challenged by the first soldier or guard who heard your accent and saw your clothes.</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Wiscard" target="Imperial Purple" id="0">
      <data key="d12">ENEMY_OF</data>
      <data key="d13">0.8</data>
      <data key="d14">our last viceroy – the same Wiscard, whose remnants still prey on the commerce among the Red Stars – aimed at the Imperial Purple.</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Wiscard" target="commerce among the Red Stars" id="0">
      <data key="d12">PARTICIPATES_IN</data>
      <data key="d13">0.7</data>
      <data key="d14">Wiscard, whose remnants still prey on the commerce among the Red Stars</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Wiscard" target="personal domain of his august majesty, the Emperor" id="0">
      <data key="d12">ENEMY_OF</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">Wiscard, whose remnants still prey on the commerce among the Red Stars – aimed at the Imperial Purple.</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Wiscard" target="Siwenna" id="0">
      <data key="d12">LOCATED_IN</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">Wiscard left Siwenna, barely ahead of us, and the planet, and with it the province, were thrown open to the admiral with every gesture of loyalty to the Emperor.</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="admiral" target="personal domain of his august majesty, the Emperor" id="0">
      <data key="d12">WORKS_FOR</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">the Emperor and his admiral</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="admiral" target="viceroy" id="0">
      <data key="d12">LEADS</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">the admiral became the new viceroy</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="viceroy" target="Emperor's crown" id="0">
      <data key="d12">LOVES</data>
      <data key="d13">0.8</data>
      <data key="d14">Our new viceroy would not refuse the Crown if offered</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="viceroy" target="daughter" id="0">
      <data key="d12">FAMILY_OF</data>
      <data key="d13">0.7</data>
      <data key="d14">he has already given one of his daughters as wife to a Kinglet</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="viceroy" target="plans to carve out a new Empire" id="0">
      <data key="d12">PARTICIPATES_IN</data>
      <data key="d13">0.8</data>
      <data key="d14">he plans to carve out a new Empire in the Barbarian hinterland</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="sixth son" target="viceroy's personal fleet" id="0">
      <data key="d12">PARTICIPATES_IN</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">He is a gunner in the viceroy's personal fleet</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="sixth son" target="Barr" id="0">
      <data key="d12">FAMILY_OF</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">What of your sixth son?</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="old man" target="history of nucleics" id="0">
      <data key="d12">MENTIONED_IN</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">"I was a scholar, and I know that in all the history of nucleics, no portable force-shield was ever invented."</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="force-shields" target="powerhouses" id="0">
      <data key="d12">LOCATED_IN</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">"We have force-shields – huge, lumbering powerhouses that will protect a city, or even a ship, but not one, single man."</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="strange men" target="stories" id="0">
      <data key="d12">PARTICIPATES_IN</data>
      <data key="d13">0.8</data>
      <data key="d14">"There have been stories percolating through space. They travel strange paths and become distorted with every parsec, –but when I was young there was a small ship of strange men, who did not know our customs and could not tell where they came from."</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="magicians" target="edge of the Galaxy" id="0">
      <data key="d12">LOCATED_IN</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">"They talked of magicians at the edge of the Galaxy; magicians who glowed in the darkness, who flew unaided through the air, and whom weapons would not touch."</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="tech-men" target="a specialized group" id="0">
      <data key="d12">MEMBER_OF</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">A specialized group which supervises the power plants.</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="tech-men" target="power plants" id="0">
      <data key="d12">SUPERVISES</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">A specialized group which supervises the power plants.</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="tech-men" target="small city stations" id="0">
      <data key="d12">CONTROLS</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">They're controlled by the tech-men.</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="tech-man" target="Foundation series" id="0">
      <data key="d12">MENTIONED_IN</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">The tech-man was short</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="tech-man" target="Siwenna" id="0">
      <data key="d12">ENEMY_OF</data>
      <data key="d13">0.8</data>
      <data key="d14">you dogs of Siwenna – and probably your strangerhood is assumed for safety's sake – are being daily punished for your rebellion</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="tech-man" target="tech-man's guild" id="0">
      <data key="d12">MEMBER_OF</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">privileges and protections of the tech-man's guild</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="tech-man" target="Siwennese traitors" id="0">
      <data key="d12">ENEMY_OF</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">The Siwennese traitors that preceded me would have – perhaps!</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="tech-man" target="University of Trantor" id="0">
      <data key="d12">WORKS_FOR</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">I studied under the great Bier at the University of Trantor</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="tech-man" target="University of Trantor" id="1">
      <data key="d12">PARTICIPATES_IN</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">I studied under the great Bier at the University of Trantor</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="tech-man" target="powerhouse" id="0">
      <data key="d12">WORKS_FOR</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">the tech-man said in strangled tones, "Have you had enough? I couldn't trust my underlings in this case."</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="tech-man" target="generators" id="0">
      <data key="d12">OWNS</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">"And all those generators are in your hands?" "Every one," said the tech-man, with more than a touch of complacency.</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Bier" target="University of Trantor" id="0">
      <data key="d12">WORKS_FOR</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">I studied under the great Bier at the University of Trantor</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Jael" target="Mallow" id="0">
      <data key="d12">KNOWS</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">"Don't stop. I want your thoughts."</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Jael" target="Minister of Education and Propaganda" id="0">
      <data key="d12">WORKS_FOR</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">What did I make you Minister of Education and Propaganda for?</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Jael" target="Foundation series" id="0">
      <data key="d12">MENTIONED_IN</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">Sutt was at the window, his back to Mallow and Jael.</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Ankor Jael" target="Jorane Sutt" id="0">
      <data key="d12">ENEMY_OF</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">you were booted out of your cabinet seat by Jorane Sutt, the same fellow who'd rather lose an eyeball than see me in the council.</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Ankor Jael" target="cabinet" id="0">
      <data key="d12">WORKS_FOR</data>
      <data key="d13">0.8</data>
      <data key="d14">you were booted out of your cabinet seat by Jorane Sutt</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Ankor Jael" target="Mallow" id="0">
      <data key="d12">KNOWS</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">Mallow looked up as Ankor Jael re-entered the room. Mallow said, "Did you hear him?"</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Ankor Jael" target="Hober Mallow" id="0">
      <data key="d12">KNOWS</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">Ankor Jael made his way into the chamber with the near-futile aid and exertions of the police department, and then through the scarcely smaller confusion within to Hober Mallow's seat. Mallow turned with relief, "By Seldon, you cut it thin. Have you got it?" "Here, take it," said Jael.</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Ankor Jael" target="EVENT" id="0">
      <data key="d12">PARTICIPATES_IN</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">Ankor Jael, from his bench on the left, made the adjustments, and with a preliminary click, a holographic scene sprang to view</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Ankor Jael" target="Foundation series" id="0">
      <data key="d12">MENTIONED_IN</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">Mallow looked about for Ankor Jael</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Korellian government" target="priest" id="0">
      <data key="d12">USES</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">He was obviously used by the Korellian government as a bait, whether involuntary or not.</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="K S P" target="Visual Record" id="0">
      <data key="d12">MENTIONED_IN</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">The light had become a set of fuzzy, glowing letters: K S P.</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="K S P" target="Foundation series" id="0">
      <data key="d12">MENTIONED_IN</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">K S P stands for 'Korellian Secret Police.'</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="K S P" target="Korell" id="0">
      <data key="d12">LOCATED_IN</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">K S P stands for 'Korellian Secret Police.'</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Asper Argo" target="Korellian Republic" id="0">
      <data key="d12">LEADS</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">Asper Argo, the Well-Beloved, Commdor of the Korellian Republic</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Dark Nebula" target="Empire" id="0">
      <data key="d12">MEMBER_OF</data>
      <data key="d13">0.8</data>
      <data key="d14">It was a ship, but a whale to the Dark Nebula's minnow; and on its side was the Spaceship-and-Sun of the Empire.</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Dark Nebula" target="warning of danger" id="0">
      <data key="d12">PARTICIPATES_IN</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">The orders went out, and the Dark Nebula prepared to run if it could, and fight if it must, –while down in the hyperwave room, a message stormed its way through hyperspace to the Foundation. Over and over again! Partly a plea for help, but mainly a warning of danger.</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="viceroy of the Normannic Sector" target="creating dissension in the Periphery" id="0">
      <data key="d12">INTERESTED_IN</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">The viceroy of the Normannic Sector is interested in creating dissension in the Periphery for his own benefit</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Republic of Korell" target="surrendered unconditionally" id="0">
      <data key="d12">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d13">0.9</data>
      <data key="d14">the Republic of Korell surrendered unconditionally</data>
    </edge>
  </graph>
